    {
      "id": "ENGINE-EXECUTION-FRAGILE",
      "title": "The edge does not survive being traded late",
      "severity": "medium",
      "severity_rank": 2,
      "detail": "Trading the same book one period later retains 58% of the Sharpe (1.42 to 0.82 annualised). An edge that depends on executing at the moment the signal is computed is an artifact of the backtest's timing assumptions rather than a property of the market, and no real book is filled that promptly.",
      "remediation": "Re-run the backtest with a realistic execution lag for the venue and report that as the headline result. If the edge only exists at zero delay, it is not an edge.",
